/*  FUNCTION NAME:      ARROWMOVES
    DESCRIPTION:*//**Returns an 8x2 moves table combining DEFAULTARROWS and _dirAll: {arrow, packed delta}.*/
/*  RETURNS:            2-column array {arrow glyph, packed delta (row*_mult+col)}, 8 rows clockwise from north
    PARAMETERS:
    EXAMPLE:            =ARROWMOVES() -> 8x2 array: col 1 is the arrow char, col 2 its packed delta (↑ = -1000000, → = 1)
    REVISIONS:          Date        Developer   Description
                        2026-04-15  Claude      Initial version
                        2026-08-20  Claude      Row order now follows the canonical clockwise-from-north order (inherited from DEFAULTARROWS / DEFAULTMOVEDELTAS)
                        2026-11-09  Claude      Help table removed from the formula; its text is the header metadata the argument hints read (#381, #382)
                        2026-11-09  Claude      Now an 8x2 {glyph, packed delta} table (HSTACK of DEFAULTARROWS and _dirAll), was 8x3 {glyph, dRow, dCol}; DEFAULTMOVEDELTAS retired (#425)
*/
ARROWMOVES = LAMBDA(
    LET(
    //  Procedure
        result, HSTACK(DEFAULTARROWS(), _dirAll),
        result
)
);
